# Installation

Paneform WM runs on macOS with a local `wm` CLI and service. Start with the local checks, then install and start the service.

## Install and start

Install the CLI using the current project release instructions. Once `wm` is available, register the service:

### installation commands

```text
wm service install
wm service start
```

### Grant permissions

The window manager needs macOS Accessibility permission to control windows and Screen Recording permission to observe them. Run `wm permissions-request` to request access, then use `wm doctor` to check the result.

### Check the service

Run `wm service status` to see whether the service is running. The [doctor reference](/wm/docs/commands/diagnostics/doctor/) explains the local permission check.

## Next steps

Read about [workspaces and layout](/wm/docs/concepts/), or try a [window move](/wm/docs/commands/windows/move-directional/) in the simulator.
